---
code: K0004
title: Invalid Escape
description: "Unrecognized escape sequence inside a double-quoted string literal"
severity: ERROR
since: 0.1.0
category: parse
tags: [parse, lexer, string, escape]
deprecated: False
---

An unrecognized escape sequence was found inside a double-quoted string literal.

Backslashes (`\`) inside strings introduce character escapes, and any character following `\` that is not one of Kura's supported escape codes triggers this error.

Supported escape sequences in Kura strings:
- [`\n`]{.expected} (newline) and [`\t`]{.expected} (tab)
- [`\\`]{.expected} (literal backslash) and [`\"`]{.expected} (literal double quote)
- [`\{`]{.expected} and [`\}`]{.expected} (literal curly braces, preventing string interpolation)

Example of erroneous code:

```kura
let path = "C:\users\kura\ui.kura"
```

To represent a literal backslash, escape the backslash itself with [`\\`]{.expected}:

```kura
let path = "C:\\users\\kura\\ui.kura"
```
